# R10: The Daydreamer (a Wayward Haint). Speaker haint_daydreamer; quest haint_daydreamer; flags haint_daydreamer_*. Region ghostlight_express.
# Four ways to end it: the token (toad_faced_stone), the Help menu (eight one-shot approaches: six listed at DC 12, two generic at DC 15; three that land
# free it, three that fall flat turn it hostile), a bottle, or a fight. Every approach is spent whatever its result (per-option flag).
# Drafted by Gemini (Gemini/sent_05_haint_daydreamer.txt, reply_05_haint_daydreamer.json), edited; see README.md.

~ start
if flag.haint_daydreamer_done or flag.haint_daydreamer_destroyed
-> END
endif
if flag.haint_daydreamer_met
-> return
endif
set haint_daydreamer_met
quest haint_daydreamer met
if quest.ghostlight_express == phantom_struck
quest ghostlight_express haints
endif
Narrator: A pale boy sits surrounded by towers of steaming pies and sugared plums, his cheeks stuffed so full they shine. He pats his empty coat pockets between bites, lookin for a weight that isn't there.
haint_daydreamer [smile]: You can have the lemon tarts if you want, because I asked for six and then I asked for twelve and they just keep coming! Do not mind the crumbs on the seat, I was checking my pockets again.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Easy there, little cub, you will choke yourself at that pace.
interject name:tobin_hayward: A lad digging in his pockets that hard has lost his best seed.
haint_daydreamer [sad]: My pocket had a hole or maybe the train took it, so I am eating cherry cobbler until I forget what was in there.
-> menu

~ return
if flag.haint_daydreamer_hostile
-> END
endif
haint_daydreamer [smile]: Oh, you came back, and the pudding is still warm if you want a bowl! I checked under the napkin three times while you were gone, just in case.
-> menu

~ menu
* How did you end up here eating all this? -> ask_story
* What would it take for you to stop eating? -> ask_want
* [if item:toad_faced_stone] Look what we found. Is this your toad stone? -> token_give
* Let us sit with you and help sort this out. -> help_open
* [if item:marble_jar or item:empty_whiskey_bottle] Set an empty glass jar open on the table between the pies. -> bottled
* Draw a weapon and strike at the ghost. -> fight
* Haints who stay on this train get burned as engine fuel. -> told_the_truth
* We will leave you to your meal. -> leave

~ ask_story
haint_daydreamer [neutral]: Well, there were cabbages in the yard next door, big green ones like cabbages always are, and a stone sat right by the gate.
haint_daydreamer [smile]: Somebody painted a green toad face on it with big yellow eyes, and it was smiling right at me, and nobody was looking out the window.
haint_daydreamer [sad]: I only put it in my coat to show it my room, and nobody ever knew it was me. Then I got on the train and it was still in my pocket, and now my pocket is empty and the pudding tastes like nothing.
-> menu

~ ask_want
haint_daydreamer [sad]: If I still had that smiling toad stone, I could walk right up the path and set it back by the cabbages.
haint_daydreamer [weary]: I cannot go back empty-handed and say I took it AND I lost it, so I have to stay right here and finish the pancakes.
-> menu

~ token_give
haint_daydreamer [afraid]: Wait a minute, wipe the jam off my eyes, is that the yellow paint right there on the chin?
haint_daydreamer [smile]: You found him! He did not fall off the train into the fog at all, he was just hiding from me!
-> token_freed

~ token_freed
haint_daydreamer [smile]: He is heavy, just like I remember, and the paint is barely chipped on his nose.
haint_daydreamer [neutral]: I am full now, I do not think I want another bite of pie.
haint_daydreamer [sad]: I am going to walk up to the porch and knock on the door and tell them I was the one who took him from the gate.
Narrator: The boy presses the painted stone to his chest and thins into sweet kitchen steam, leavin nothing on the booth but clean white plates.
take toad_faced_stone
set haint_daydreamer_done
set haint_daydreamer_how = "token"
quest haint_daydreamer token
approve tobin_hayward +1 lucan_houndstooth +1: You helped a lost boy give back what he took
narrate haint:freed_sting
narrate haint:heal
give clockwork_amulet
narrate haint:keepsake_daydreamer
set gl_after_recount = "router"
-> ghostlight_express/haint_common:recount

~ help_open
haint_daydreamer [weary]: You can sit down if you want, while I try the custard. I do not see how talking puts a stone back in a pocket, though.
-> help

~ help
# E7: a tool check (Painter's Supplies); until then an ability check gated by the kit
* [if not flag.haint_daydreamer_used_painters_supplies and item:painters_supplies] [Wisdom DC 12] Let me paint a little toad on a pebble for you. -> painters_supplies_ok | painters_supplies_miss
# E7: a tool check (Forgery Kit); until then an ability check gated by the kit
* [if not flag.haint_daydreamer_used_forgery and item:forgery_kit] [Dexterity DC 12] Let us write a neat apology note together right now. -> forgery_ok | forgery_miss
* [if not flag.haint_daydreamer_used_insight] [Insight DC 12] It is not the missing stone that scares you, is it? -> insight_ok | insight_miss
* [if not flag.haint_daydreamer_used_persuasion] [Persuasion DC 12] Neighbours forgive a brave boy who tells the truth. -> persuasion_ok | persuasion_miss
* [if not flag.haint_daydreamer_used_history] [History DC 12] Every grown-up has taken something small once and felt sorry. -> history_ok | history_miss
* [if not flag.haint_daydreamer_used_investigation] [Investigation DC 12] Walk me through the last moment you felt it in your pocket. -> investigation_ok | investigation_miss
* [if not flag.haint_daydreamer_used_performance] [Performance DC 15] Pretend I am your neighbour. Walk up and tell me. -> performance_ok | performance_miss
* [if not flag.haint_daydreamer_used_nature] [Nature DC 15] Let us talk about garden toads and why they miss home. -> nature_ok | nature_miss
* Step back for now. -> menu

~ painters_supplies_ok
set haint_daydreamer_used_painters_supplies
set haint_daydreamer_wins += 1
Narrator: You take up a brush and dab of pigment, coaxing a wide yellow-eyed grin onto a smooth bit of pebble.
haint_daydreamer [smile]: Look at his silly mouth, that is almost the exact same green! He is just a little rock with paint on him, isn't he, not a whole monster.
-> tally

~ painters_supplies_miss
set haint_daydreamer_used_painters_supplies
set haint_daydreamer_fails += 1
Narrator: You try to sketch a toad's face onto a saucer, but the glaze blurs the paint into a muddy smudge.
haint_daydreamer [sad]: That does not look like him at all, his eyes were round and bright and that just looks like spilled gravy.
-> tally

~ forgery_ok
set haint_daydreamer_used_forgery
set haint_daydreamer_wins += 1
Narrator: You smooth a clean leaf of paper beside the plates and pen a neat, earnest letter in a nine-year-old's round hand.
haint_daydreamer [smile]: You spelled all the big words right and everything, and it still looks like my writing! If I hand this over first, my throat will not close up when I try to talk.
-> tally

~ forgery_miss
set haint_daydreamer_used_forgery
set haint_daydreamer_fails += 1
Narrator: You draft a formal apology on a stiff card, heavy with tall flourishes and courtroom ink.
haint_daydreamer [weary]: Nobody would ever believe I wrote that, they would think I stole a lawyer's letter too.
-> tally

~ insight_ok
set haint_daydreamer_used_insight
set haint_daydreamer_wins += 1
Narrator: You lean across the white tablecloth, looking past the jam-stained cheeks to the small, hunched shoulders.
haint_daydreamer [sad]: I am not even scared they will yell at me about the rock. I just do not want them to look at me and know I am a thief.
-> tally

~ insight_miss
set haint_daydreamer_used_insight
set haint_daydreamer_fails += 1
Narrator: You watch the boy's darting eyes and guess aloud about the dishes and the train.
haint_daydreamer [neutral]: No, the pie is real good, I just like pie, you do not know anything about my pockets.
-> tally

~ persuasion_ok
set haint_daydreamer_used_persuasion
set haint_daydreamer_wins += 1
Narrator: You speak softly over the clatter of silver, steady and warm as a kitchen hearth.
haint_daydreamer [smile]: Do you really think they would be glad just to hear the truth? Maybe they missed talking to me more than they missed the rock.
-> tally

~ persuasion_miss
set haint_daydreamer_used_persuasion
set haint_daydreamer_fails += 1
Narrator: You offer a brisk lecture on honesty and the duties of a good neighbour.
haint_daydreamer [weary]: You sound like a schoolbook, and schoolbooks do not know how big the front porch looks when you are in trouble.
-> tally

~ history_ok
set haint_daydreamer_used_history
set haint_daydreamer_wins += 1
Narrator: You share an old, quiet tale of grown folk who pocketed small treasures in your youth and carried the weight for years.
haint_daydreamer [smile]: Really, even tall people with boots and jobs took things from gardens once? I thought I was the only bad one on the whole street.
-> tally

~ history_miss
set haint_daydreamer_used_history
set haint_daydreamer_fails += 1
Narrator: You recite a dry account of petty thefts and village magistrates from long ago.
haint_daydreamer [sad]: Did they put those people in the dark? I think I want some more roast beef right now.
-> tally

~ investigation_ok
set haint_daydreamer_used_investigation
set haint_daydreamer_wins += 1
Narrator: You tap the brass rail and trace the boy's path from the carriage door to the booth, checking every seam and cushion.
haint_daydreamer [neutral]: Wait, I remember I had my hand on it when the clowns went by, before I ever sat down here! I did not lose it forever, I just dropped it in the other car.
-> tally

~ investigation_miss
set haint_daydreamer_used_investigation
set haint_daydreamer_fails += 1
Narrator: You turn the tablecloth corners and peer beneath the stacked saucers, rattling the silverware.
haint_daydreamer [weary]: I already looked under the plates a hundred times, you are just getting syrup on your sleeves.
-> tally

~ performance_ok
set haint_daydreamer_used_performance
set haint_daydreamer_wins += 1
Narrator: You stand in the aisle and play the neighbour at the garden gate, tipping an imaginary hat with a kindly nod.
haint_daydreamer [smile]: And then I say I am sorry I took your toad, and you say thank you for telling me! That was easy when we practiced it.
-> tally

~ performance_miss
set haint_daydreamer_used_performance
set haint_daydreamer_fails += 1
Narrator: You put on a booming, theatrical voice to play the neighbour answering the door.
haint_daydreamer [afraid]: Do not do that voice, you are making it scarier than it already is!
-> tally

~ nature_ok
set haint_daydreamer_used_nature
set haint_daydreamer_wins += 1
Narrator: You murmur of damp garden moss and cool stones, and how every toad knows the smell of its own patch of earth.
haint_daydreamer [smile]: A garden toad belongs under the cabbage leaves where the bugs are, not rattling around in a coat on a train. Even if I cannot carry him back myself, I ought to go tell them where he went.
-> tally

~ nature_miss
set haint_daydreamer_used_nature
set haint_daydreamer_fails += 1
Narrator: You explain the habits of pond frogs and the shedding of skins in springtime.
haint_daydreamer [neutral]: He is made out of rock, silly, he does not eat flies or swim in ditches.
-> tally

~ tally
if flag.haint_daydreamer_wins >= 3
-> helped_freed
endif
if flag.haint_daydreamer_fails >= 3
-> turns_hostile
endif
-> help

~ helped_freed
haint_daydreamer [neutral]: My stomach does not hurt anymore, and I do not think I need the rest of this cake.
haint_daydreamer [smile]: You are nice for sitting with me, even if we did not have the stone in our hands.
haint_daydreamer [sad]: Telling the truth is the part that matters anyway, so I am going to go knock on that door right now.
Narrator: He slides down from the velvet seat and dissolves into a drift of warm cinnamon air, leavin the booth quiet and still.
set haint_daydreamer_done
set haint_daydreamer_how = "helped"
quest haint_daydreamer helped
approve lucan_houndstooth +1 tobin_hayward +1: You talked a guilty boy round to owning up
narrate haint:freed_sting
narrate haint:heal
give clockwork_amulet
narrate haint:keepsake_daydreamer
set gl_after_recount = "router"
-> ghostlight_express/haint_common:recount

~ turns_hostile
haint_daydreamer [angry]: Stop talking to me, you are ruining the taste of everything and making me think about it!
haint_daydreamer [afraid]: You just want me to be in trouble forever, so get away from my table!
Narrator: The child lets out a shrill, rattling wail that curdles the cream on the plates, and the brass lamps dim in a sudden frost.
set haint_daydreamer_hostile
quest haint_daydreamer hostile
combat gl_haint_daydreamer

~ told_the_truth
set told_haints_soul_coal
haint_daydreamer [afraid]: Burn me up in the engine? No, the frogman with the fiddle said we were all riding to the end of the line!
haint_daydreamer [angry]: You are lying to scare me, or the whole train is a trap, and I will not let you throw me in the fire!
Narrator: Plates shatter against the floor as his terror sharpens into a freezing wail, and the carriage air turns bitter as ash.
approve rook_coldwake -2 tobin_hayward -2 silas_vane -2: You told a ghost that it would be burned for fuel
set haint_daydreamer_hostile
quest haint_daydreamer hostile
combat gl_haint_daydreamer

~ fight
narrate haint:wail
approve cordelia_skein -1 rook_coldwake -1: You struck a haint first
set haint_daydreamer_hostile
quest haint_daydreamer hostile
combat gl_haint_daydreamer

~ bottled
haint_daydreamer [afraid]: Hey, the table is spinning and I was not done with my pie yet!
Narrator: Pale light swirls into the glass until the cork seats itself with a soft pop, like a small breath caught and held.
if item:marble_jar
take marble_jar
else
take empty_whiskey_bottle
endif
give bottled_haint_daydreamer
set gl_bottled += 1
set haint_daydreamer_done
set haint_daydreamer_how = "bottled"
quest haint_daydreamer bottled
narrate haint:bottle_carried
set gl_after_recount = "router"
-> ghostlight_express/haint_common:recount

~ leave
haint_daydreamer [weary]: Pass me that gravy boat before you go, even though it does not taste like anything.
-> END
